    "body": "Well, remember https://whatwg.org/faq#adding-new-features; let's not jump straight to specific solutions. I tried to reframe your OP in terms of use cases, instead of solutions. (Step 2.) Assuming I did so accurately, let's brainstorm other ways of accomplishing those use cases:\r\n\r\n- We could add a way to use registerProtocolHandler() with a scope, so that it only applies to your page or site.\r\n- We could add back isProtocolHandlerRegistered(), which would allow you to test if a protocol handler is present, and only rewrite the href=\"\"s if there is no such registered.\r\n\r\nBoth of these seem to accomplish the use case (\"third path\") I listed above.\r\n\r\nBy the way, per the adding new features process, the main work still to do here is step 3.",
